<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What Android may carry out of this application, from Android 12 on:
    nothing, by either of the two ways it asks.

    `android:allowBackup="false"` in the manifest answers for the cloud, and
    that is the only thing it answers for. Android's own documentation is plain
    about it: for an application targeting Android 12 or later, on the devices
    of some manufacturers, that attribute turns down the backup to the cloud
    and leaves the device-to-device transfer running. That transfer is not an
    attacker — it is the user setting up a new telephone — but it copies
    whatever it has not been told to leave behind, and SPEC §8 has the two
    places somebody names for themselves (§7.6) written on the device, read on
    the device, erased on the device, and sent nowhere. A telephone one no
    longer holds is nowhere.

    So every domain Android knows how to extract is excluded, one by one, in
    both sections: what is not named here is taken, and an omission would be a
    decision nobody took. The four `device_` domains name the direct-boot
    storage, which this application does not use; they are named all the same,
    so that the rule holds whole rather than resting on that staying true.

    Nothing is included, and nothing is meant to be. The datasets are
    downloaded again in a few minutes, the settings are a few taps, and neither
    is worth carrying to another telephone without being asked.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
